<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Performance on each dataset of RoBERTa-Base with different <math id="A5.T8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{token\_num}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>token</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>num</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{token\_num}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The upper part includes STSB, while the lower part excludes STSB (STSB is denoted as “–”).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Further analysis on <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{token\_num}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>token</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>num</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{token\_num}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
As shown in the Figure <a href="#S5.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ 5.2 The Shape of FDAs ‣ 5 Ablation and Explorative Study ‣ Model Merging with Functional Dual Anchors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, we observe that the average performance decreases when the <math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{token\_num}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>token</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>num</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{token\_num}</annotation></semantics></math> increases from <math id="A5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> for RoBERTa-Base models, which appears to contradict the trends observed in ViT-B/32. We further analyze the performance of each dataset. As shown in Table <a href="#A5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix E More Results and Discussions for Section ‣ Appendix ‣ Model Merging with Functional Dual Anchors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, we find that the performance drop is mainly attributed to STSB. Therefore, we conduct merging without STSB and observe that the performance consistently increases with larger <math id="A5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{token\_num}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>token</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>num</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{token\_num}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is consistent with the trend in ViT-B/32. We hypothesize that FDAs yield better performance when their shape is closer to that of the real data space.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
